## Problem classes

### `Destructive fallback wipes nets`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| User networks gone after upgrade | `fallbackToDestructiveMigration()` | Real `Migration` for every version bump; register all prior migrations |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Pin lost on REPLACE upsert`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| Main pin clears after edit/save | `OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE` writes defaults | Merge from existing row: keep `createdAt` / `isPinnedMain` unless caller intentionally changes them |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `Link mode reset on SIM refresh`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| User set mobile link to VPN; later becomes PROXY | Metadata upsert overwrote `mode` | Merge: new row → PROXY default; existing → keep `mode`, update label/slot/icc only |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->

### `KSP2 Unit signature V`

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
| ------- | ----- | --- |
| KSP fails: `unexpected jvm signature V` on Room DAOs | Room 2.6.x + KSP 2.3 (KSP2) mishandles Kotlin `Unit`/void on suspend DAOs | Room **2.7.x** (pin 2.7.2). Do not drop KSP2 or delete suspend DAO methods. |

<!-- last-verified: 2026-08 -->
